When a plain Tab accepts a writing suggestion, Ladybird fires its
keydown with the keyCode 229 and with isComposing set, as for a key an
input method takes. Of the other engines, only WebKit shows macOS
writing suggestions inline. Its WebViewImpl::showInlinePredictionsFor-
Candidate() hands them to “showCompletionForCandidate:” of
NSSpellChecker, which draws them without marked text. And its
KeyboardEvent takes isComposing from Editor::hasComposition(), in
viewIsCompositing(), so going by WebKit’s source alone, its keydown for
that Tab has isComposing false. Chromium and Gecko have no inline-
completion code in their macOS widget layers. With isComposing set, Tab
accepts the suggestion in GitHub’s comment fields, which would
otherwise type a tab themselves.
